 Needs Python 3.8+.
 
+## Measure a page after an SEO edit
+
+Export two separate periods for the same Search Console property with the same filters. For example, use the 28 days before a title change and the 28 days after it. Pass the later export first and the earlier one after `--before`.
+
+```bash
+python3 gsc_striking_distance.py after.zip --before before.zip \
+  --page 'https://carlens.ca/blog/how-to-negotiate-a-used-car-price-canada'
+```
+
+Open `page-comparison.md` to see clicks, impressions, CTR and average position before and after, with the change beside each pair. Copy the exact page URL from `Pages.csv`. A dash means a value is unavailable. A row missing from one export has unknown performance for that period.
+
+Leave out `--page` to follow all earlier striking-distance pages, including ones that later move above or below the ranking window. Markdown shows the first `--top` pages (15 by default). Add `--csv out/` for the full list in `out/page-comparison.csv`. CTR changes are in percentage points, and a move from position 9.6 to 6.1 is a change of −3.5. These are observed changes across the two periods. Other factors can affect search performance over the same dates.
+
 ## Real example
 
 [`examples/carlens-report.md`](examples/carlens-report.md) is the output for [carlens.ca](https://carlens.ca), a used-car listing checker I built, using 3 months of data (Aug–Oct 2026). Highlights:
